1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:05,033
♪ In the not too
distant future ♪

2
00:00:05,033 --> 00:00:08,200
♪ Somewhere in time and space ♪

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:11,200
♪ Mike Nelson and
his robot pals ♪

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,500
♪ Are caught in
an endless chase ♪

5
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,500
♪ Pursued by a woman
whose name is Pearl ♪

6
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,433
♪ An evil gal who wants
to rule the world ♪

7
00:00:20,433 --> 00:00:23,233
♪ She threw a few
things in her purse ♪

8
00:00:23,233 --> 00:00:25,167
♪ And in her rocket
ship she hunts him ♪

9
00:00:25,167 --> 00:00:27,167
♪ All across the universe ♪

10
00:00:27,167 --> 00:00:30,067
- [Pearl] I'll get you!

11
00:00:30,067 --> 00:00:33,033
♪ I'll send him cheesy movies ♪

12
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:36,367
♪ The worst I can
find, la la la ♪

13
00:00:36,367 --> 00:00:39,133
♪ He'll have to sit
and watch them all ♪

14
00:00:39,133 --> 00:00:42,333
♪ And I'll monitor
his mind, la la la ♪

15
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:45,367
♪ Now keep in mind
Mike can't control ♪

16
00:00:45,367 --> 00:00:48,733
♪ Where the movies
begin or end, la la la ♪

17
00:00:48,733 --> 00:00:51,400
♪ He'll try to keep his sanity ♪

18
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:56,367
♪ With the help of
his robot friends ♪

19
00:00:57,167 --> 00:00:58,167
♪ Robot Roll Call ♪

20
00:00:58,167 --> 00:00:59,700
- Cambot!
- You're on!

21
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:00,900
- Gypsy!
- Oh my stars!

22
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:02,800
- Tom Servo!
- Check me out!

23
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:04,300
- Crow!
- I'm different!

24
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:07,233
♪ If you're wondering how
he eats and breathes ♪

25
00:01:07,233 --> 00:01:10,367
♪ And other science
facts, la la la ♪

26
00:01:10,367 --> 00:01:13,567
♪ Just repeat to yourself,
it's just a show ♪

27
00:01:13,567 --> 00:01:16,567
♪ I should really just relax ♪

28
00:01:16,567 --> 00:01:20,800
♪ For Mystery Science
Theater 3000 ♪

29
00:01:23,467 --> 00:01:26,233
(doors slamming)

30
00:01:35,867 --> 00:01:37,900
- Hey everyone, welcome
to the Satellite of Love.

31
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:40,333
You know, since we are stuck
in orbit over ancient Rome,

32
00:01:40,333 --> 00:01:42,333
I thought it might be a
good time to teach the bots

33
00:01:42,333 --> 00:01:43,867
a little something
about history.

34
00:01:43,867 --> 00:01:46,100
- Mike, this
encyclopedia is worthless

35
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:47,700
for my biography of Roland Gift.

36
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:49,033
- Yeah, Mike, it's really old.

37
00:01:49,033 --> 00:01:51,533
It lists Hitler as a
fairly stable veteran

38
00:01:51,533 --> 00:01:53,333
of the Great War.
- Oh come on,

39
00:01:53,333 --> 00:01:54,933
they're not that
old, they're fine.

40
00:01:54,933 --> 00:01:56,433
- Oh yeah?

41
00:01:56,433 --> 00:01:57,767
It mentions the light
bulb as a charming theory.

42
00:01:57,767 --> 00:01:59,733
- Yeah, and congress
is spelled with an F.

43
00:01:59,733 --> 00:02:01,300
What is a gongreff?

44
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:04,033
- Well I used 'em when I was
a kid, they seemed fine then.

45
00:02:04,033 --> 00:02:06,800
- The periodic table has
three elements in it, Mike!

46
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:08,833
- There's a volume for
the letter epsilon.

47
00:02:08,833 --> 00:02:11,133
- There's a mailing
address for Machu Picchu.

48
00:02:11,133 --> 00:02:12,967
- It's got a picture
of Stonehenge.

49
00:02:12,967 --> 00:02:14,000
- So?

50
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,433
- Under construction.
- Yeah.

51
00:02:15,433 --> 00:02:18,233
- Oh, well, so what you
high-minded encyclopedia snobs

52
00:02:18,233 --> 00:02:20,067
are trying to tell me
is you want a new set.

53
00:02:20,067 --> 00:02:21,300
Fine, I'll get you a new set.

54
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:22,933
- Anything that's not
hand written on papyrus

55
00:02:22,933 --> 00:02:24,200
will do.
- Yeah.

56
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:25,533
- That's very funny,
we'll be right back.

57
00:02:25,533 --> 00:02:28,000
You know, they got
me through college.

58
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,100
- You never finished
college, Mike.

59
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:31,933
- Oh yeah.
(Crow sighing)

60
00:02:31,933 --> 00:02:34,500
(upbeat music)

61
00:02:39,333 --> 00:02:42,367
- I mean, look, some day
we hope to harness fire

62
00:02:42,367 --> 00:02:44,833
to serve man, not
simply terrorize him

63
00:02:44,833 --> 00:02:46,200
with horrifying randomness.

64
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:48,033
- Yeah, yeah, and
here's a whole section

65
00:02:48,033 --> 00:02:50,600
on our deadly foes,
the dinosaurs.

66
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:52,767
(Mike groaning)
- Okay, you bellyachers,

67
00:02:52,767 --> 00:02:56,833
got you a brand-spanking-new
set of encyclopedias,

68
00:02:56,833 --> 00:02:58,700
each page with an
internet up link

69
00:02:58,700 --> 00:03:00,633
so you can constantly
update 'em.

70
00:03:00,633 --> 00:03:02,700
- Man, this is
incredibly up to date.

71
00:03:02,700 --> 00:03:06,167
- Wow, 27 pages on
Gwen Stefani alone.

72
00:03:06,167 --> 00:03:07,667
- Amazing.
- Well, I think I've more

73
00:03:07,667 --> 00:03:10,433
than answered your
encyclopedia grievances.

74
00:03:10,433 --> 00:03:11,900
- No.
- No!

75
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:13,467
It was much more fun to
complain about the old ones

76
00:03:13,467 --> 00:03:14,833
than to have new ones.

77
00:03:14,833 --> 00:03:17,600
- Yeah, yeah, I miss
complaining already, frankly.

78
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:19,600
- I gotta check in on
that planet down there,

79
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:20,733
down there you know?

80
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:24,633
(vocalizing)

81
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:27,833
- Thank you, Maximus.

82
00:03:27,833 --> 00:03:29,133
Oh, hi Mike.

83
00:03:29,133 --> 00:03:30,667
Well, this whole Roman thing

84
00:03:30,667 --> 00:03:32,800
has taken a turn for the crappy.

85
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:35,700
Flavia here discovered
we weren't gods and all

86
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:38,500
and had us thrown into
this slimy dungeon.

87
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:41,233
And they're being pretty
rough on pale face here,

88
00:03:41,233 --> 00:03:44,167
they took away his brain
which sucks for him.

89
00:03:44,167 --> 00:03:47,200
- I like fruit, fruit is good.

90
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:49,000
- [Flavia] Talk, hirsute one.

91
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:52,133
Do you plot against
our beloved Emperor?

92
00:03:52,133 --> 00:03:54,100
- [Bobo] Oh, please, I
can't stand it anymore!

93
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:56,533
(crying)
- And Bobo, man,

94
00:03:56,533 --> 00:03:59,533
they are totally
torturing him right now.

95
00:03:59,533 --> 00:04:01,633
I mean, it's bad, Mike.

96
00:04:01,633 --> 00:04:05,233
You guys should probably
write to Amnesty International

97
00:04:05,233 --> 00:04:07,900
House of Pancakes or whatever.

98
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,233
Oh, I broke a nail.

99
00:04:10,233 --> 00:04:13,500
(Bobo hooting)
(Woman laughing)

100
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:16,000
- Talk, smelly fake god.

101
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,967
- I'll say anything
you want, just give me

102
00:04:17,967 --> 00:04:19,433
some of that yummy mutton!

103
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:21,767
- Is it safe?

104
00:04:21,767 --> 00:04:23,167
- I don't care if it's
safe, it smells delicious!

105
00:04:23,167 --> 00:04:25,467
Give me!
- Treasonous fool!

106
00:04:26,667 --> 00:04:28,100
- The Emperor's about to
give his violin recital

107
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:30,100
upstairs, ma'am.
- Ooh, right.

108
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:32,967
Listen, I must go
but I'll be back

109
00:04:32,967 --> 00:04:36,667
and you three will
be like so tortured,

110
00:04:36,667 --> 00:04:39,767
it's like not even funny.
(laughing)

111
00:04:39,767 --> 00:04:40,600
- No, no!

112
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:45,633
- So, Mike, here's the deal.

113
00:04:45,633 --> 00:04:47,133
If you help us out of this one,

114
00:04:47,133 --> 00:04:51,267
I promise I'll let you and
your little wind up toys go

115
00:04:51,267 --> 00:04:54,900
and you'll never have to watch
another lousy movie again.

116
00:04:57,167 --> 00:04:58,500
- Yes, yes, do it, Mike!
- No more crummy movies?

117
00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:00,100
- Do it, come on!
- Do it, do it!

118
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:01,100
- Hey, hey, hey, hey!
- Yes, yes, yes, yes!

119
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:02,567
- [Both] Hey, hey, hey!

120
00:05:02,567 --> 00:05:05,267
- I don't know, Pearl, I mean
you've lied to us before.

121
00:05:05,267 --> 00:05:07,133
- I know!

122
00:05:08,267 --> 00:05:11,100
But it wasn't my fault,

123
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:14,667
in a way that I haven't
quite figured out yet.

124
00:05:14,667 --> 00:05:18,367
But this time for real.

125
00:05:18,367 --> 00:05:20,500
I mean, how are you gonna
get out of this stupid,

126
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:23,000
stinky Roman time
without us anyway?

127
00:05:24,533 --> 00:05:25,767
- She's right, Mike.

128
00:05:25,767 --> 00:05:27,567
I don't wanna have
to see you in toga.

129
00:05:27,567 --> 00:05:29,433
(shuddering)
- I don't know.

130
00:05:29,433 --> 00:05:31,033
Okay, what do you want me to do?

131
00:05:32,467 --> 00:05:34,833
- I need you to come down
here and get brain guy's

132
00:05:34,833 --> 00:05:37,733
brain for us, they put
it too far out of range

133
00:05:37,733 --> 00:05:39,700
so he's at quarter
power, which means

134
00:05:39,700 --> 00:05:42,533
he's even more of
an idiot than usual.

135
00:05:42,533 --> 00:05:45,133
- Pearl, tell me about
the rabbits again, please?

136
00:05:45,133 --> 00:05:47,933
- And pathetic as it
is, he's our only hope,

137
00:05:47,933 --> 00:05:50,900
so I'm gonna have him bring
you down here to fetch it.

138
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:53,667
Okay, brain guy, send Mike down.

139
00:05:53,667 --> 00:05:55,400
- Send Mike down.

140
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:56,233
Okay.

141
00:05:58,233 --> 00:06:00,400
- Oh, dude!
(sneezing)

142
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:01,633
I'm allergic.

143
00:06:01,633 --> 00:06:04,867
- Not goose down, you dope!

144
00:06:04,867 --> 00:06:07,100
Bring Mike down!

145
00:06:08,267 --> 00:06:10,667
- Mike, everyone says
you're ugly and dumb

146
00:06:10,667 --> 00:06:13,400
and no one likes you.
(chuckling)

147
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:14,567
(Mike chuckling)
- Oh come on,

148
00:06:14,567 --> 00:06:16,767
they do not, really?

149
00:06:17,900 --> 00:06:18,733
Oh man, really?

150
00:06:20,033 --> 00:06:22,233
Oh man, that really
brought me down.

151
00:06:24,867 --> 00:06:26,033
- Mike.
(chuckling)

152
00:06:26,033 --> 00:06:28,633
- Listen, you
empty-headed albino,

153
00:06:28,633 --> 00:06:32,767
I said bring Mike down here!

154
00:06:32,767 --> 00:06:34,300
- Okay, nice lady.

155
00:06:36,967 --> 00:06:38,467
- Oh, my, what am I doing here?

156
00:06:38,467 --> 00:06:41,867
I was just at a 401K
planning meeting.

157
00:06:41,867 --> 00:06:45,167
Oh, by the way, my name's
Mike Down, I'm a CPA.

158
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,633
(clanging)
(Observer groaning)

159
00:06:48,633 --> 00:06:49,867
- Thank you.

160
00:06:49,867 --> 00:06:52,000
- This might take
a minute, Mike.

161
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,900
In the meantime,
why don't you enjoy

162
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:57,433
your final bad movie
ever, I promise.

163
00:06:57,433 --> 00:07:00,667
It's a real piece of
cheese called Space Mutiny.

164
00:07:00,667 --> 00:07:05,067
Hey, brain low, think you
can manage sending a movie?

165
00:07:05,067 --> 00:07:05,900
- Okay.

166
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:09,833
- Should I set up my
overhead projector now?

167
00:07:09,833 --> 00:07:11,700
- You pipe down.

168
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:12,900
(alarm blaring)
- Movie!

169
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:14,000
- Maybe Carter likes
me or something.

170
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,967
Ooh, Gypsy likes me, that's it!

171
00:07:15,967 --> 00:07:18,700
(doors clanging)

172
00:07:26,767 --> 00:07:29,767
(suspenseful music)

173
00:07:30,967 --> 00:07:33,167
- [Tom] Amazingly
Idiotic Productions.

174
00:07:33,167 --> 00:07:35,200
(chuckling)

175
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:36,067
- [Mike] That's good.

176
00:07:38,767 --> 00:07:42,167
- [Crow] A Jonathan Winters,
Billie Holiday production.

177
00:07:42,167 --> 00:07:45,733
(awe-inspiring music)

178
00:07:45,733 --> 00:07:47,100
(gasping)

179
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:49,200
- David Winters.
- Oh, we're in good hands.

180
00:07:52,633 --> 00:07:55,133
- [Tom] 20 exclusive hits
by the original artists!

181
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:57,867
- [Mike] Sounds like
someone owns himself

182
00:07:57,867 --> 00:07:59,833
a DX7 keyboard, huh?

183
00:08:01,067 --> 00:08:03,067
- [Crow] Whoa, whoa,
watch out, watch out!

184
00:08:05,167 --> 00:08:08,200
- [Tom] I have my doubts that
this movie is starring anyone.

185
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:09,467
- [Mike] It's just
the usual stable

186
00:08:09,467 --> 00:08:10,767
of David Winters' actors.

187
00:08:14,467 --> 00:08:15,833
- [Tom] Yay, oh, no, wait.

188
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:20,233
Oh, because she's
Cameron Mitchell's, wait.

189
00:08:21,233 --> 00:08:22,733
- [Crow] His nickname is Tiny.

190
00:08:24,233 --> 00:08:25,633
- [Tom] Featuring
music normally heard

191
00:08:25,633 --> 00:08:28,233
at the Days Inn lounge
in Columbia Heights.

192
00:08:28,233 --> 00:08:31,733
(awe-inspiring music)

193
00:08:31,733 --> 00:08:33,400
- [Mike] Passed from
editor to editor

194
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:35,233
in a desperate
attempt to save it.

195
00:08:40,633 --> 00:08:41,967
- [Crow] There's gonna
be seven levels of Hell

196
00:08:41,967 --> 00:08:43,067
in this movie too.

197
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:48,200
- [Tom] Deb, big favor,
can you associate produce?

198
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:49,033
Thanks.

199
00:08:50,567 --> 00:08:52,433
- [Crow] Hope John
and Holiday DeKock?

200
00:08:52,433 --> 00:08:53,833
- [Mike] What
kinda name is that?

201
00:08:58,100 --> 00:09:00,567
And completely botched
by David Winters.

202
00:09:03,467 --> 00:09:05,767
- [Tom] Outlets in space.

203
00:09:05,767 --> 00:09:08,167
- 13 generations ago--
- Wow.

204
00:09:08,167 --> 00:09:11,300
- [Narrator] Our overpopulated
world built the Southern Sun.

205
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:12,633
- [Mike] No we didn't.

206
00:09:12,633 --> 00:09:13,933
- [Narrator] A
self-sufficient spaceship

207
00:09:13,933 --> 00:09:17,100
that would be home to
thousands of migrants.

208
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:19,400
With a 10-light-year
journey to a new

209
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:22,267
and un-colonized world.
- Cool, huh?

210
00:09:22,267 --> 00:09:24,233
- [Narrator] Our current
descendants have come to accept

211
00:09:24,233 --> 00:09:26,500
the Southern Sun as their home

212
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:28,767
and work for a better
future for their children.

213
00:09:28,767 --> 00:09:30,700
- [Mike] They're known as dupes.

214
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:31,900
- [Narrator] While
most of the inhabitants

215
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:33,700
of this generation are content,

216
00:09:35,067 --> 00:09:38,800
there are some who have
grown restless and impatient.

217
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:41,000
- [Tom] Like Pat Riley
here, for instance.

218
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,567
(suspenseful music)

219
00:09:44,567 --> 00:09:47,533
- [Crow] Where the hell did I
put that old ping pong table?

220
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:50,667
- [Mike] I have this
feeling I'm being followed

221
00:09:50,667 --> 00:09:54,200
by a lobster boy.
(Tom chuckling)

222
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:56,867
- [Crow] Still, he's
not nearly as creepy

223
00:09:56,867 --> 00:09:58,267
as most meter readers.

224
00:10:01,267 --> 00:10:03,733
- [Tom] He's like an
Armand Assante wannabe.

225
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:10,300
- [Mike] Show you how to
use a label maker properly.

226
00:10:13,633 --> 00:10:16,800
- [Crow] He made a bomb out
of soap and Paco Rabanne.

227
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:20,233
- [Announcer] Attention, prepare
for shuttle lancer landing.

228
00:10:20,233 --> 00:10:21,500
- [Mike] Melissa Manchester!

229
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:23,133
- [Pilot] Lancer
to Southern Sun,

230
00:10:23,133 --> 00:10:24,833
located rescue
beacon and survivors,

231
00:10:24,833 --> 00:10:28,000
they're all female and identify
themselves as Bellerians.

232
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,600
We have initiated
landing procedures

233
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:31,067
and are returning to base.

234
00:10:31,067 --> 00:10:32,467
- [Tom] I could watch
this stuff all day, Mike.

235
00:10:32,467 --> 00:10:34,267
- [Mike] Oh, you will.

236
00:10:34,267 --> 00:10:35,667
- [Lemont] You will
enter the Southern Sun

237
00:10:35,667 --> 00:10:37,467
in figures five millennium

238
00:10:37,467 --> 00:10:40,267
and your docking bay
is one niner, over.

239
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:42,900
- [Pilot] Roger,
shuttle lancer locked

240
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:44,633
to guidance control, over.

241
00:10:44,633 --> 00:10:46,133
(vocalizing)

242
00:10:46,133 --> 00:10:50,133
♪ Lame ♪
(vocalizing)

243
00:10:50,133 --> 00:10:52,600
- [Mike] Shuttle craft
determined to be cute, sir.

244
00:10:55,467 --> 00:10:56,867
(beeping)

245
00:10:56,867 --> 00:10:58,733
- [Pilot] Shuttle
landing successful.

246
00:10:58,733 --> 00:11:00,500
Bellerian survivors
disembarking.

247
00:11:01,733 --> 00:11:03,833
- Attention, all hands.
- Dungeon.

248
00:11:03,833 --> 00:11:05,267
- [Announcer] Shuttle
landing complete.

249
00:11:05,267 --> 00:11:08,267
Prepare for incoming
Stingray Viper Squadron.

250
00:11:08,267 --> 00:11:11,300
- [Pilot] Red two,
Southern Sun in sight.

251
00:11:11,300 --> 00:11:12,367
- [Tom] S'cuse me.

252
00:11:12,367 --> 00:11:14,500
S'cuse me.
- Attention.

253
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:15,833
- S'cuse me.
- All those wishing to meet

254
00:11:15,833 --> 00:11:18,000
the incoming Viper
Squadron proceed

255
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,567
to the docking bay.
- Who's that?

256
00:11:19,567 --> 00:11:21,467
- Lea!
- Hi, Dad!

257
00:11:21,467 --> 00:11:22,900
Hi Scott.
- Hi!

258
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:24,433
- Ah, so pretty.

259
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:25,933
- If you're going down
to the docking bay

260
00:11:25,933 --> 00:11:27,567
to meet your friend from
Coreolus you better hurry.

261
00:11:27,567 --> 00:11:28,500
- Oi!

262
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:29,967
- The Viper's in final approach.

263
00:11:29,967 --> 00:11:32,467
- Well I came down to check
that he's on the flight.

264
00:11:32,467 --> 00:11:34,467
- Lieutenant Lemont!

265
00:11:34,467 --> 00:11:35,700
- Mac.
(Tom growling)

266
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:37,367
- Contact the pilot
of the Stingray Viper

267
00:11:37,367 --> 00:11:39,700
and ask if Professor
Spooner is aboard.

268
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:42,100
- I'm insane!
- Thank you.

269
00:11:42,100 --> 00:11:44,733
- Sun Control, I have a request.

270
00:11:44,733 --> 00:11:46,500
Do you have a Professor
Spooner on board?

271
00:11:46,500 --> 00:11:48,533
Over.
- Stingray to Sun Control,

272
00:11:48,533 --> 00:11:50,100
affirmative, over.

273
00:11:50,100 --> 00:11:52,033
- [Crow] Sting, Debbie
Reynolds and God.

274
00:11:52,033 --> 00:11:52,933
- Bye, Dad.
- Bye bye.

275
00:11:52,933 --> 00:11:54,133
- Bye, Scott.
- Bye.

276
00:11:54,133 --> 00:11:55,400
- [Pilot] Southern Sun,

277
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:57,433
we are starting our
landing sequence.

278
00:11:57,433 --> 00:12:00,167
- [Mike] In the future,
geese will be rocket powered.

279
00:12:00,167 --> 00:12:01,400
- [Stingray Two] Southern
Sun, abort landing,

280
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:03,467
we have pirates coming
up fast on our tail!

281
00:12:04,900 --> 00:12:06,667
Stingray Two to Stingray
Three, we are under fire,

282
00:12:06,667 --> 00:12:08,500
prepare for defense formation.

283
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:09,767
- [Stingray Three]
Roger, Stingray Two.

284
00:12:09,767 --> 00:12:11,133
- [Tom] Graphics by Kenner.

285
00:12:12,567 --> 00:12:14,367
- [Stingray One] Stingray One,
assuming defense formation,

286
00:12:14,367 --> 00:12:16,033
we'll cover for you
and the professor.

287
00:12:16,033 --> 00:12:17,500
(alarms blaring)

288
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:19,900
- What the hell's
going on out there?

289
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:21,200
- [Pilot] Look out, Red Three!

290
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:22,400
Red Three is down.

291
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:24,400
- [Crow] I never liked
Red Three anyway.

292
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:25,200
- Damn it!

293
00:12:28,467 --> 00:12:30,533
(vocalizing)
♪ Crap ♪

294
00:12:30,533 --> 00:12:32,133
- [Pilot] Pirate
ship eliminated.

295
00:12:32,133 --> 00:12:35,800
- [Mike] Special effects by
Industrial Light and Morons.

296
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:39,167
(lasers firing)

297
00:12:39,167 --> 00:12:40,400
- [Pilot] Good shot, Ryder.

298
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:42,667
- [Tom] Are we the good
guys or the bad guys?

299
00:12:42,667 --> 00:12:44,100
- [Announcer]
Attention, all hands,

300
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:46,367
man your battle stations,
we're under attack.

301
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,500
- [Mike] Uh-oh, an air
show, look out below!

302
00:12:53,033 --> 00:12:55,433
- [Crow] I told you we
should've landed at LaGuardia.

303
00:12:57,900 --> 00:13:00,400
Tell me about it, these
briefs I'm wearin' huh?

304
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:01,800
(Tom chuckling)

305
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:03,833
- [Mike] So their spaceship
has a huge basement.

306
00:13:04,833 --> 00:13:06,233
(Tom humming)

307
00:13:06,233 --> 00:13:07,300
- [Tom] Say...

308
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:10,300
- [Man] Commander
Kalgan, can I help you?

309
00:13:10,300 --> 00:13:11,633
- [Crow] Calgon?

310
00:13:11,633 --> 00:13:14,367
- Excuse me, Sir.
- Did you have a reservation?

311
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:17,667
- [Man] Commander, Sir,
what are you doing?

312
00:13:18,667 --> 00:13:20,233
(beeping)

313
00:13:20,233 --> 00:13:23,533
- [Mike] The hostess will
seat you in a moment, sir!

314
00:13:23,533 --> 00:13:28,300
We have a perfectly fine bar
if you'd like to wait there.

315
00:13:28,300 --> 00:13:29,800
Oh, I see.

316
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:31,533
Oh great, yeah, shooting
me is not gonna get you to

317
00:13:31,533 --> 00:13:34,967
a table any faster, sir.
(man groaning)

318
00:13:34,967 --> 00:13:36,967
I'll get the manager.

319
00:13:36,967 --> 00:13:39,133
- [Tom] Kalgan, blow me away.

320
00:13:39,133 --> 00:13:41,700
(upbeat music)

321
00:13:46,467 --> 00:13:49,367
- [Mike] Does that guy inflate
his pants to attract mates?

322
00:13:50,533 --> 00:13:52,000
(exploding)

323
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,333
- [Tom] Good work, you
blew up the septic tank.

324
00:13:56,033 --> 00:13:58,233
- [Crow] Oh no, I just tried
to open my garage door,

325
00:13:58,233 --> 00:13:59,033
what the?

326
00:14:00,667 --> 00:14:01,867
(beeping)

327
00:14:01,867 --> 00:14:04,000
- [Computer] Warning,
system power loss.

328
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,267
- [Tom] Too right!

329
00:14:05,267 --> 00:14:07,567
- Energize our
emergency landing strip.

330
00:14:07,567 --> 00:14:09,000
- We're off circuit!

331
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,667
It's dead, sir.
- Guidance system failing!

332
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:13,833
(Tom laughing)

333
00:14:13,833 --> 00:14:15,033
- We lost power!

334
00:14:15,033 --> 00:14:16,900
- [Mike] Relax, you're
in your own room.

335
00:14:16,900 --> 00:14:21,400
- We lost power!
(static hissing)

336
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:24,000
- [Tom] Is it a good idea for
a pilot to eject in space?

337
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:25,767
- [Computer] Viper out of
control, collision imminent.

338
00:14:25,767 --> 00:14:29,067
Pilot emergency beam down
ejection system activated.

339
00:14:29,067 --> 00:14:30,433
- Attention all hands,
(Tom hissing)

340
00:14:30,433 --> 00:14:33,400
prepare for crash landing.
(ship exploding)

341
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:34,800
- [Crow] So really,
how does this help

342
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:37,067
the Basque separatists?
(man yelling)

343
00:14:37,067 --> 00:14:38,567
- Scott!
- My stair stepper!

344
00:14:39,967 --> 00:14:41,600
- [Announcer] Attention,
pilot beam down successful.

345
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:44,833
Medical team, stand by,
fire control to docking bay.

346
00:14:44,833 --> 00:14:47,767
(explosion booming)
(Tom chuckling)

347
00:14:47,767 --> 00:14:50,733
- Look out, it's gonna blow!
(Mike laughing)

348
00:14:50,733 --> 00:14:52,200
It's gonna blow!

349
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:53,400
- [Tom] If the first 10
minutes are any indication,

350
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:55,167
this movie's gonna blow!

351
00:14:55,167 --> 00:14:56,600
(crew yelling)

352
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:58,900
- [Crow] My Buns of Steel
videos are in there!

353
00:14:58,900 --> 00:15:00,600
- We have to get him!
- We don't have time!

354
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:03,367
- It's gonna blow!
- He'll burn alive!

355
00:15:03,367 --> 00:15:06,100
- It's gonna blow!
- Come on, Mother.

356
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:10,167
(ship exploding)

357
00:15:11,267 --> 00:15:15,300
- [Tom] Oh, yeah,
that'll take care of it.

358
00:15:15,300 --> 00:15:17,800
- [Lea] My god, the Professor.

359
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,567
(Kalgan chuckling)

360
00:15:21,567 --> 00:15:23,533
- [Mike] Remember
Carl's blonde joke?

361
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,633
(Kalgan laughing)

362
00:15:26,633 --> 00:15:28,167
- What happened, Lieutenant?

363
00:15:28,167 --> 00:15:30,000
- The Viper was locked into
the Sun's guidance control,

364
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,500
Commander, and we lost power!

365
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:34,500
- Commander, the energizing
turbines have been sabotaged.

366
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:35,933
- Sabotaged?

367
00:15:35,933 --> 00:15:38,167
- [Tom] But what of the little
children and their toys?

368
00:15:39,433 --> 00:15:40,767
- [Crow] John Waters.

369
00:15:41,667 --> 00:15:43,733
- Headquarters.
- Blake here.

370
00:15:43,733 --> 00:15:46,067
Give me Kalgan.
- He's right here, go ahead.

371
00:15:46,067 --> 00:15:49,300
- Sir, I just saw something I
thought you should know about.

372
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:52,333
Some strange women came
on board with the Lancer.

373
00:15:52,333 --> 00:15:53,533
- Strange women.
- I'm sorry the information

374
00:15:53,533 --> 00:15:55,033
is so scanty, but I'll
send you up more--

375
00:15:55,033 --> 00:15:57,133
- Scanty?
- As I get it.

376
00:15:57,133 --> 00:15:57,967
Blake out.

377
00:15:59,533 --> 00:16:01,267
- [Mike] Hey, look at
this, the office newsletter

378
00:16:01,267 --> 00:16:03,033
says I look like Susan Powter.

379
00:16:04,433 --> 00:16:06,300
- [Tom] Santa's playing
FreeCell over here.

380
00:16:06,300 --> 00:16:09,200
(computer beeping)

381
00:16:12,633 --> 00:16:14,833
- Oh man, what'd I do?
- What do you think, Devers?

382
00:16:14,833 --> 00:16:17,900
- [Crow] Should I spend
20 bucks for Griffey?

383
00:16:17,900 --> 00:16:20,900
- I think whoever did this knows
his way around space ships.

384
00:16:20,900 --> 00:16:22,567
- I agree.
- I don't know if this helps

385
00:16:22,567 --> 00:16:24,867
but ho ho ho.
- On thing's for sure,

386
00:16:24,867 --> 00:16:26,733
we've gotta reduce
speed drastically

387
00:16:26,733 --> 00:16:28,900
'til we repair the damage.

388
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:33,633
You know, I'm thinking more
about the possible motive.

389
00:16:33,633 --> 00:16:34,833
Why?
(Tom laughing)

390
00:16:34,833 --> 00:16:35,800
- Commander?
- Ho?

391
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:39,067
- Ho.
- You get a computer readout

392
00:16:39,067 --> 00:16:41,600
on the damage in
the docking bay.

393
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:43,533
Also, the pirate
fleet's position

394
00:16:43,533 --> 00:16:46,167
and load the file
into the computer.

395
00:16:46,167 --> 00:16:48,633
I'd like to do some research
on our new female guests,

396
00:16:48,633 --> 00:16:50,467
the Bellerians.
- Nude research!

397
00:16:50,467 --> 00:16:53,000
- I want that ready
as soon as possible.

398
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:55,067
- Aye aye, Sir.
- Thank you, Devers.

399
00:16:56,033 --> 00:16:59,667
(mysterious music)

400
00:16:59,667 --> 00:17:01,867
- [Tom] So, we've got
some Benedictine monks

401
00:17:01,867 --> 00:17:03,800
in the floorboards,
unfortunately.

402
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:06,900
We have set some traps with
fresh bread and brandy, though.

403
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:11,133
- Ladies?

404
00:17:11,133 --> 00:17:12,967
This is your new home.

405
00:17:14,467 --> 00:17:16,533
I know it doesn't
look like much,

406
00:17:16,533 --> 00:17:17,767
but if you'll bear with us,

407
00:17:17,767 --> 00:17:21,133
I'm sure we can make
you quite comfortable.

408
00:17:21,133 --> 00:17:24,367
- [Jennera] Leave, we
Bellerians wish to be alone.

409
00:17:24,367 --> 00:17:27,067
This place will
serve our purpose.

410
00:17:27,067 --> 00:17:28,267
Leave.

411
00:17:28,267 --> 00:17:29,933
- [Tom] Whoa, drank
too much Surge.

412
00:17:32,433 --> 00:17:33,800
- [Crow] Bryce, you okay?

413
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:37,200
- It's a pleasure
having you on board.

414
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:38,433
- [Tom] I guess.

415
00:17:38,433 --> 00:17:39,267
- Gentlemen.

416
00:17:40,433 --> 00:17:41,767
- [Tom] Oh, and by
the way, ladies,

417
00:17:41,767 --> 00:17:44,433
there's a ferret cage by
the wall if you need it.

418
00:17:45,900 --> 00:17:49,267
(suspenseful music)

419
00:17:49,267 --> 00:17:51,000
- [Crow] Well, I polished
the back corridor,

420
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,667
anyone else need
their room done?

421
00:17:56,633 --> 00:17:58,033
- [Mike] Hey, you
guys, I got my dad's

422
00:17:58,033 --> 00:18:01,700
Enforcer for the weekend.
(Kalgan chuckling)

423
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:03,167
- [Tom] We have fun, huh?

424
00:18:07,167 --> 00:18:09,200
- [Crow] Can you help
me out of this thing?

425
00:18:11,333 --> 00:18:13,667
- [Kalgan] Our
timing was perfect.

426
00:18:13,667 --> 00:18:15,900
Two for the price of one.
- We had a coupon.

427
00:18:17,567 --> 00:18:19,800
- Who would've thought
that one small spacecraft--

428
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:21,100
- [Crow] Robbie Robertson.

429
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:24,267
- Could've done
that much damage?

430
00:18:24,267 --> 00:18:26,400
- That Viper's missile
pod took out the entire

431
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:28,967
winching system to
the docking bay doors.

432
00:18:28,967 --> 00:18:31,700
- [Tom] Man, you
should've been there!

433
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:34,167
- According to
the damage reports

434
00:18:34,167 --> 00:18:35,967
from the Chief
Maintenance Engineer,

435
00:18:37,367 --> 00:18:39,500
it'll take at least two
weeks before the docking bay

436
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:41,833
can be used again.
- I know, it's great.

437
00:18:41,833 --> 00:18:44,000
- Couldn't have
wished for it better.

438
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,500
(Tom chuckling)

439
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:48,200
- That means the Southern
Sun is completely isolated.

440
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:49,633
(Tom snickering)

441
00:18:49,633 --> 00:18:52,000
Nobody can enter her.

442
00:18:53,133 --> 00:18:54,400
And more important,

443
00:18:55,500 --> 00:18:58,100
nobody can leave her.
(Tom laughing)

444
00:18:58,100 --> 00:18:59,533
- Excellent.

445
00:18:59,533 --> 00:19:02,600
They no longer have a choice.
(laughing)

446
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:04,800
- [Mike] God, you look good.

447
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:08,567
- It was cruel fate
to be born in space.

448
00:19:08,567 --> 00:19:10,400
But I have vowed we
will not die here.

449
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:14,367
It is my destiny to set
my feet upon a real world

450
00:19:14,367 --> 00:19:16,533
and to accumulate
wealth and power

451
00:19:16,533 --> 00:19:19,767
beyond our wildest dreams.
(chuckling)

452
00:19:19,767 --> 00:19:23,233
I have offered the people
of the Southern Sun a rich,

453
00:19:23,233 --> 00:19:25,233
new life.
- That's good.

454
00:19:25,233 --> 00:19:27,100
- And now they
have no alternative

455
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:30,700
but to accept my
generosity and alter course

456
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:33,800
for Corona Borealis.
- Ooh.

457
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:36,667
(laughing)
- Don't you love it?

458
00:19:36,667 --> 00:19:38,933
You know, we're always laughing,
you and me, it's great.

459
00:19:38,933 --> 00:19:40,200
- Lieutenant.
- Oi.

460
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:41,933
- What's the report
from damage control?

461
00:19:41,933 --> 00:19:43,867
- It's not complete
yet, Captain.

462
00:19:43,867 --> 00:19:46,400
But the first reports
indicate that two of our

463
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:48,467
(Tom hissing)
LM5000 accion drive motors

464
00:19:48,467 --> 00:19:51,033
have been sabotaged.
- Boy.

465
00:19:51,033 --> 00:19:52,600
- This also affects
the performance

466
00:19:52,600 --> 00:19:55,133
of one of our vixon
piles drive generators.

467
00:19:55,133 --> 00:19:57,100
- Oi.
- Give me a computer readout

468
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:59,700
on our whole stress factor.
- Sir.

469
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:01,967
- [Devers] Reduce
speed by two thirds.

470
00:20:01,967 --> 00:20:03,933
Shut down two of
our booster engines.

471
00:20:03,933 --> 00:20:06,333
- Yes, sir.
- Oh, one other thing.

472
00:20:06,333 --> 00:20:07,800
- [Crow] Oi!

473
00:20:07,800 --> 00:20:09,500
- Can you establish video
contact with the docking bay?

474
00:20:10,667 --> 00:20:12,267
- One of the missiles
from the Viper took out

475
00:20:12,267 --> 00:20:14,667
the video control
tower down there.

476
00:20:14,667 --> 00:20:16,833
But we are trying to
reestablish contact

477
00:20:16,833 --> 00:20:18,167
with a sarid video robot.

478
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:21,167
- [Tom] Did you sign
Sherry's birthday card?

479
00:20:21,167 --> 00:20:23,500
(dramatic music)

480
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:26,167
- We've been in space too long!

481
00:20:26,167 --> 00:20:28,033
Let us land the ship.

482
00:20:28,033 --> 00:20:30,367
We can do it, we have the power!

483
00:20:30,367 --> 00:20:32,667
- It's true, we have
the power to do this!

484
00:20:32,667 --> 00:20:34,100
- Yes.
- But this would directly

485
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,800
oppose the law of the universe!

486
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:37,567
- Yes.
- The law of the galaxy!

487
00:20:37,567 --> 00:20:39,367
- Forget the law!
- No!

488
00:20:39,367 --> 00:20:42,133
No, the law must be
upheld, we cannot break it.

489
00:20:42,133 --> 00:20:45,233
- Oh, okay so we--
- Gentlemen.

490
00:20:45,233 --> 00:20:48,567
It seems that we are
not all in agreement.

491
00:20:48,567 --> 00:20:49,500
- [Tom] I disagree!

492
00:20:50,733 --> 00:20:53,733
- Engineer Parsons
seems content to spend

493
00:20:53,733 --> 00:20:56,733
his remaining years
upon the Southern Sun.

494
00:20:56,733 --> 00:20:58,733
- Then let him do so, alone.

495
00:20:58,733 --> 00:21:00,633
- [Man] Yeah, that's right!

496
00:21:00,633 --> 00:21:02,233
- This is mutiny,
this is treason,

497
00:21:02,233 --> 00:21:03,800
which I warn you, I must report.

498
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:05,500
- [Crow] I just have
to wet myself first.

499
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:08,400
- Will you allow him

500
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:12,933
to spoil your ambitions
for a greater future?

501
00:21:12,933 --> 00:21:14,200
- [Man] Not allow that!

502
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:15,800
- [Tom] The easily
led wise council.

503
00:21:17,700 --> 00:21:19,600
- [Mike] What I meant
was I totally endorse

504
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:20,900
what you're doing, ow!

505
00:21:21,833 --> 00:21:23,067
- [Crow] Rip his band uniform,

506
00:21:23,067 --> 00:21:24,633
then he'll have to pay for it!

507
00:21:24,633 --> 00:21:25,633
- [Tom] Next they're
gonna give him books

508
00:21:25,633 --> 00:21:27,000
so they can dump 'em.

509
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:29,067
- Okay.
- Right over here.

510
00:21:29,067 --> 00:21:31,633
- [Crow] Death by snicker-snag.

511
00:21:31,633 --> 00:21:33,867
- [Man] Hold him, hold him.

512
00:21:35,900 --> 00:21:38,100
- [Mike] I'm gonna
inflate him to 35 pounds.

513
00:21:41,167 --> 00:21:43,800
- [Tom] Okay, then, moving on
to number three on our agenda,

514
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:47,200
Sherry's birthday party.
- Are there any other of you

515
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:51,033
that wish to confuse
freedom with treason?

516
00:21:51,033 --> 00:21:54,233
- [Mike] I'd like to confuse
bok choy with cabbage, sir.

517
00:21:54,233 --> 00:21:56,333
- Report to the
Enforcer's bridge.

518
00:21:56,333 --> 00:21:57,567
- Let's go, hurry up!

519
00:21:57,567 --> 00:21:58,833
- [Crow] Well it
is the rare meeting

520
00:21:58,833 --> 00:22:00,533
where something
actually got done.

521
00:22:01,467 --> 00:22:02,800
- [Mike] You're strict, sir.

522
00:22:03,833 --> 00:22:05,600
- You have done well.

523
00:22:05,600 --> 00:22:08,367
(doors clanging)

524
00:22:20,067 --> 00:22:21,400
- Alone at last.

525
00:22:23,233 --> 00:22:25,400
(humming)

526
00:22:32,533 --> 00:22:36,200
(gentle instrumental music)

527
00:22:50,067 --> 00:22:52,200
(sighing)

528
00:22:58,133 --> 00:23:01,100
(crashing)
The hell?

529
00:23:01,100 --> 00:23:04,067
- [Crow] Red Norvo, Red Norvo,
this is Goldilocks Niner,

530
00:23:04,067 --> 00:23:06,967
I'm coming in sucker,
prepare to die.

531
00:23:06,967 --> 00:23:09,400
- [Tom] Oh yeah,
well come get some!

532
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:11,867
(explosion booming)
- Crow, Servo,

533
00:23:11,867 --> 00:23:14,000
what the hell in
Michigan is going on?

534
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:15,300
- [Crow] I can't talk now, Mike,

535
00:23:15,300 --> 00:23:17,833
I'm locked in a death
struggle with Servo.

536
00:23:17,833 --> 00:23:20,900
- [Tom] Yeah, me too,
Mike, only with Crow, over.

537
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:23,067
- Cambot, give me rocket
number nine, will ya?

538
00:23:23,067 --> 00:23:25,133
- [Crow] Eat death, Servo!

539
00:23:25,133 --> 00:23:28,333
- [Tom] Eat munchy crunchy
chocolatey cocoa death, Crow!

540
00:23:28,333 --> 00:23:31,500
- [Crow] Enjoy a nice serving
of ground Betty with death,

541
00:23:31,500 --> 00:23:36,400
but mostly eat death.
(explosion booming)

542
00:23:36,400 --> 00:23:37,400
- Crow, Servo?

543
00:23:37,400 --> 00:23:39,033
You guys be careful out there.

544
00:23:39,033 --> 00:23:40,200
- [Crow] Oh, we won't.

545
00:23:41,300 --> 00:23:42,967
(groaning)

546
00:23:42,967 --> 00:23:45,233
Servo, you just ripped
a hole in my torso.

547
00:23:45,233 --> 00:23:46,067
Wee!

548
00:23:47,100 --> 00:23:48,533
(Tom groaning)

549
00:23:48,533 --> 00:23:50,967
- [Tom] Too late for me, I
took a laser blast to the dome.

550
00:23:50,967 --> 00:23:53,400
Wahoo!
- Fellas?

551
00:23:53,400 --> 00:23:55,333
- [Tom] Well, shall we
auger these babies in?

552
00:23:55,333 --> 00:23:56,267
- [Crow] After you.

553
00:23:57,833 --> 00:24:02,800
- I love you, Crow!
- I'm sorta fond of you Servo!

554
00:24:03,533 --> 00:24:06,367
(explosion booming)

555
00:24:07,333 --> 00:24:10,033
- Crow, Servo, you guys okay?

556
00:24:12,367 --> 00:24:13,200
Fellas?

557
00:24:14,400 --> 00:24:17,133
(fire crackling)

558
00:24:20,733 --> 00:24:23,167
Okay, now this
isn't funny anymore.

559
00:24:23,167 --> 00:24:24,767
(Tom laughing)

560
00:24:24,767 --> 00:24:26,533
- Lighten up, Nelson,
we're robots, remember?

561
00:24:26,533 --> 00:24:28,167
- Man, that was great.
- Yeah!

562
00:24:28,167 --> 00:24:29,967
- So where'd you
get the space ships?

563
00:24:29,967 --> 00:24:32,067
- Oh, you mean the hyper
warp escape shuttles

564
00:24:32,067 --> 00:24:33,600
which we just trashed?

565
00:24:33,600 --> 00:24:34,867
- Yeah, those.
- Oh, they've been down

566
00:24:34,867 --> 00:24:36,567
in the hold waiting for
us to use 'em to escape

567
00:24:36,567 --> 00:24:38,567
and stuff like that.
- Oh, I see.

568
00:24:38,567 --> 00:24:40,067
- Yeah.
- So don't you think

569
00:24:40,067 --> 00:24:41,867
we maybe should've used
them for escape purposes?

570
00:24:41,867 --> 00:24:43,967
- What purposes?
- What's he on about?

571
00:24:43,967 --> 00:24:46,067
- Oh, you mean escape from here.

572
00:24:46,067 --> 00:24:47,200
- Oh!
- Oh geez.

573
00:24:47,200 --> 00:24:48,733
How stupid of us, Mike, man.

574
00:24:48,733 --> 00:24:50,600
- Boy, is my face red.

575
00:24:50,600 --> 00:24:51,800
Sorry Mike.
- Oh boy.

576
00:24:51,800 --> 00:24:53,433
- We had escape pods,
we didn't use 'em.

577
00:24:53,433 --> 00:24:55,400
- Wait, isn't there
just one more?

578
00:24:55,400 --> 00:24:56,567
- Oh yeah, Gypsy's got it out,

579
00:24:56,567 --> 00:24:57,800
she'll be along any second now.

580
00:24:57,800 --> 00:25:00,500
- [Gypsy] For England
and the Queen!

581
00:25:00,500 --> 00:25:02,833
- All right, go for it, Gyps!

582
00:25:02,833 --> 00:25:04,533
Take it in.
- We'll be right back.

583
00:25:04,533 --> 00:25:07,133
(upbeat music)

584
00:25:11,467 --> 00:25:13,000
- Oh that was fun!
- That was great, man.

585
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:14,933
- Scott Devers.
- Dave Ryder.

586
00:25:14,933 --> 00:25:16,400
- Pleased to me
you, shall we do it?

587
00:25:16,400 --> 00:25:17,800
- [Tom] Oh, this is sudden.

588
00:25:19,600 --> 00:25:20,833
- Lieutenant.
- Sir?

589
00:25:20,833 --> 00:25:22,567
- Please file this.
- Certainly, sir.

590
00:25:22,567 --> 00:25:24,100
- Thank you.

591
00:25:24,100 --> 00:25:25,600
- [Mike] You know where I
could get some Zubaz, man?

592
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:28,800
- Commander Jansen.
- Well, welcome aboard,

593
00:25:28,800 --> 00:25:31,600
Mr. Ryder, you've met
our Captain, Devers?

594
00:25:31,600 --> 00:25:33,067
Sit down, son.
- Thank you, sir.

595
00:25:33,067 --> 00:25:36,467
- All right and could I have
your space status card, please?

596
00:25:36,467 --> 00:25:38,467
Thank you.
- Sorry it's so moist.

597
00:25:39,500 --> 00:25:41,333
(beeping)

598
00:25:41,333 --> 00:25:42,533
- [Tom] You've got mail.

599
00:25:44,867 --> 00:25:47,467
- Well there we have it,
any questions, Mr. Ryder?

600
00:25:47,467 --> 00:25:49,800
- Sir, I'd like to see a
video of the crash, if I may.

601
00:25:49,800 --> 00:25:51,467
- Good idea, come this way.

602
00:25:51,467 --> 00:25:52,833
- [Tom] I'll show
you where my elves

603
00:25:52,833 --> 00:25:54,867
are working day and night.
- Take a chair.

604
00:25:54,867 --> 00:25:55,867
- [Crow] And ram it.

605
00:25:57,000 --> 00:25:59,000
(murmuring)

606
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:00,500
- Lieutenant.
- Yes, sir?

607
00:26:00,500 --> 00:26:02,767
- Could you punch up a
video of the crash, please?

608
00:26:02,767 --> 00:26:05,133
- Yes sir.
- On our computer.

609
00:26:05,133 --> 00:26:06,733
- [Computer] Disaster analysis.

610
00:26:06,733 --> 00:26:09,100
Guidance system engaged.

611
00:26:09,100 --> 00:26:10,267
You are now on the--
- Oi?

612
00:26:10,267 --> 00:26:11,633
- Southern Sun's guidance--
- Ho.

613
00:26:11,633 --> 00:26:12,867
- Control system, over.

614
00:26:12,867 --> 00:26:14,333
Pilot control released.

615
00:26:14,333 --> 00:26:16,033
Warning, critical power loss.

616
00:26:17,900 --> 00:26:20,200
- [Tom] We now switch
live to Spencer's Gifts.

617
00:26:23,133 --> 00:26:25,900
- [Mike] Hey Macarena.

618
00:26:28,800 --> 00:26:33,267
- [Tom] Ayyyy.
(Mike laughing)

619
00:26:33,267 --> 00:26:35,833
- [Crow] It's a Wicca
Tupperware party.

620
00:26:35,833 --> 00:26:38,767
(mysterious music)

621
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:41,433
- [Mike] Steve called?

622
00:26:41,433 --> 00:26:42,533
- [Crow] My poultice.

623
00:26:44,833 --> 00:26:47,533
- [Mike] Oh, I've got this
itch right on my leg there.

624
00:26:48,833 --> 00:26:49,900
- [Crow] Look familiar, Mike?

625
00:26:49,900 --> 00:26:52,200
Oh, what am I saying, no way.

626
00:26:52,200 --> 00:26:53,300
- [Mike] Hey.

627
00:26:54,600 --> 00:26:56,467
- [Tom] Damn Swedish
ergonomic chairs,

628
00:26:56,467 --> 00:26:58,267
how do you sit
comfortably on these?

629
00:27:00,933 --> 00:27:02,200
- [Crow] Get a bunch
of women together,

630
00:27:02,200 --> 00:27:04,500
it's either witchery
or a wedding shower.

631
00:27:04,500 --> 00:27:05,400
That's what I say.

632
00:27:06,533 --> 00:27:08,933
- [Tom] Mother
Angelica aerobics.

633
00:27:10,433 --> 00:27:11,533
- [Mike] I heard that.

634
00:27:16,267 --> 00:27:18,367
- [Crow] I better get
the phone, you guys.

635
00:27:20,433 --> 00:27:22,300
- [Jennera] You
received our message.

636
00:27:22,300 --> 00:27:25,000
I'm glad you've come,
we've been waiting for you.

637
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:27,333
- [Man] Hey you, the
Bellerians are off limits.

638
00:27:27,333 --> 00:27:29,800
- [Tom] You've never heard
of the getting some clause?

639
00:27:30,933 --> 00:27:32,500
- [Commander] Well,
there we are, gentlemen.

640
00:27:32,500 --> 00:27:34,367
Tell me, Dave--
- Slab bulkhead.

641
00:27:34,367 --> 00:27:36,367
- Your Viper was
equipped with a new

642
00:27:36,367 --> 00:27:40,000
high-density deatomizer
escape system, right?

643
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:41,500
- Yes, Commander.

644
00:27:41,500 --> 00:27:43,700
Right now it only works
over very short distances.

645
00:27:43,700 --> 00:27:46,433
But who knows what the future
potential of it could be.

646
00:27:46,433 --> 00:27:48,467
- What about the professor?
- What's his max?

647
00:27:48,467 --> 00:27:50,767
- Commander, I'm sorry
about the professor.

648
00:27:50,767 --> 00:27:52,633
There's nothing I could've done.

649
00:27:52,633 --> 00:27:55,700
The system's only hooked
up to the Viper pilot.

650
00:27:55,700 --> 00:27:57,167
- Don't blame yourself, son.

651
00:27:57,167 --> 00:27:58,700
- [Crow] It's not your
fault you're a chunk head.

652
00:27:58,700 --> 00:28:00,400
- You're lucky you're alive.

653
00:28:00,400 --> 00:28:01,967
You're lucky you saved yourself.

654
00:28:02,933 --> 00:28:04,867
- [Tom] I can't breathe.

655
00:28:04,867 --> 00:28:05,700
(groaning)

656
00:28:05,700 --> 00:28:06,833
- Lea.

657
00:28:06,833 --> 00:28:08,767
You had us all worried.

658
00:28:08,767 --> 00:28:10,433
Please, next time
there's a fire,

659
00:28:10,433 --> 00:28:12,700
leave it to damage control.

660
00:28:12,700 --> 00:28:14,600
You okay?
- Okay?

661
00:28:14,600 --> 00:28:17,633
Next time, young lady,
you stay out of the way.

662
00:28:17,633 --> 00:28:19,967
- Dad, I was there, the
pilot chickened out,

663
00:28:19,967 --> 00:28:22,933
otherwise Spooner would
be alive right now!

664
00:28:22,933 --> 00:28:26,433
- David Ryder, I want you
to meet my daughter, Lea.

665
00:28:26,433 --> 00:28:28,033
- [Mike] We're
about the same age.

666
00:28:28,033 --> 00:28:29,967
- Professor never had a chance.

667
00:28:29,967 --> 00:28:31,767
There's nothing I could've
done to prevent it.

668
00:28:31,767 --> 00:28:34,200
- Oh, so you left him to die--
- Lea!

669
00:28:34,200 --> 00:28:35,533
Stop it.

670
00:28:35,533 --> 00:28:38,267
- He ejected and he's alive!
- Listen, lady!

671
00:28:38,267 --> 00:28:39,933
- Doctor!
- Doctor!

672
00:28:39,933 --> 00:28:41,733
- Doctor Lady!
- I don't have to justify

673
00:28:41,733 --> 00:28:43,200
my actions to you!

674
00:28:43,200 --> 00:28:46,500
But since you're asking,
that explosion cut the power

675
00:28:46,500 --> 00:28:48,100
and there wasn't time to
go over to the auxiliary

676
00:28:48,100 --> 00:28:49,700
back up system!

677
00:28:49,700 --> 00:28:52,500
I had to eject, I
had no other choice!

678
00:28:52,500 --> 00:28:54,867
- [Tom] That's Doctor
I Had No Other Choice!

679
00:28:56,033 --> 00:28:58,100
- Commander, Captain,

680
00:28:58,100 --> 00:28:59,900
excuse me, I have
to file my report.

681
00:28:59,900 --> 00:29:01,100
- [Mike] Coach will
totally ream me

682
00:29:01,100 --> 00:29:02,600
if I don't file my report.

683
00:29:03,933 --> 00:29:04,767
- [Commander] Lea.

684
00:29:06,333 --> 00:29:08,233
- [Tom] You're getting
a lump of coal.

685
00:29:10,633 --> 00:29:12,600
- [Crow] I like
playing with the knobs.

686
00:29:14,300 --> 00:29:16,033
- [Mike] All you
can eat me tonight.

687
00:29:16,033 --> 00:29:17,267
- [Woman] Excuse me, sir,

688
00:29:17,267 --> 00:29:19,167
I think you'll find
this interesting.

689
00:29:19,167 --> 00:29:20,600
- Yes, what is it?

690
00:29:20,600 --> 00:29:21,767
- [Woman] It's an inventory
of all the explosives

691
00:29:21,767 --> 00:29:22,867
under our control.

692
00:29:25,033 --> 00:29:26,833
- [Tom] Hey, one
of the New Monkees.

693
00:29:29,833 --> 00:29:31,700
- [Crow] Oh, Gopher,
are you lost?

694
00:29:33,700 --> 00:29:36,100
- [Mike] He's calling
to check on his gender.

695
00:29:36,100 --> 00:29:39,000
- Give me an audio video link
of bridge to console seven.

696
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:40,500
Please hurry.

697
00:29:40,500 --> 00:29:42,000
- There's something coming
through on the voice monitor

698
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:43,733
from the engine room area.
- Wow.

699
00:29:43,733 --> 00:29:45,000
- Put it through on five.

700
00:29:47,200 --> 00:29:49,000
- [Tom] The
electrolysis is working.

701
00:29:51,667 --> 00:29:52,800
- [Crow] Those Formica monitors

702
00:29:52,800 --> 00:29:55,067
don't have a lot of resolution.

703
00:29:55,067 --> 00:29:57,100
- My name is Flight
Lieutenant Lemont.

704
00:29:57,100 --> 00:29:58,033
(Tom hissing)

705
00:29:58,033 --> 00:29:59,267
- Well according to my printout

706
00:29:59,267 --> 00:30:00,900
from the supply
store's inventory,

707
00:30:00,900 --> 00:30:04,100
we're definitely
short on conventional
ballistic explosive.

708
00:30:04,100 --> 00:30:05,900
I mean, I've double checked.

709
00:30:05,900 --> 00:30:08,367
Somebody with direct
online access to Central

710
00:30:08,367 --> 00:30:09,867
has been transferring
large amounts

711
00:30:09,867 --> 00:30:11,267
of explosives--
- Lobster.

712
00:30:11,267 --> 00:30:13,500
- And then simply
covering the requisition.

713
00:30:13,500 --> 00:30:14,767
I wouldn't have
found out about it

714
00:30:14,767 --> 00:30:16,667
unless Central asked me
to confirm acceptance

715
00:30:16,667 --> 00:30:20,067
of 100 units of chemo
plastic and atomic compound.

716
00:30:20,067 --> 00:30:21,733
I mean, that's crazy, can
you imagine that amount

717
00:30:21,733 --> 00:30:23,900
of explosives lying around
the ship's engine room?

718
00:30:23,900 --> 00:30:26,533
- [Tom] Come on, skull,
pop out of my skin.

719
00:30:26,533 --> 00:30:28,433
- [Steve] I think
I've traced who it is.

720
00:30:28,433 --> 00:30:29,567
- Who in the hell
is he talking to?

721
00:30:29,567 --> 00:30:31,800
Put it through to the bridge.

722
00:30:31,800 --> 00:30:33,667
- [Steve] I want to speak to
somebody from Command, please.

723
00:30:33,667 --> 00:30:34,933
- [Mike] Excuse me, Al Lewis.

724
00:30:34,933 --> 00:30:37,167
- Okay, for the
sake of security,

725
00:30:37,167 --> 00:30:38,467
I think it would be
better if you came up here

726
00:30:38,467 --> 00:30:41,033
and asked for me,
Lieutenant Lemont.

727
00:30:41,033 --> 00:30:42,500
- Send a couple of
men over there to stop

728
00:30:42,500 --> 00:30:45,133
that engineer before
he gets to the bridge.

729
00:30:45,133 --> 00:30:47,400
Unless I get to him first.
- Time me!

730
00:30:47,400 --> 00:30:48,200
Go ahead.

731
00:30:49,433 --> 00:30:50,467
- [Tom] Well I think I
just had to report this,

732
00:30:50,467 --> 00:30:51,800
I mean, I really
thought about it

733
00:30:51,800 --> 00:30:53,067
and I think I really
have to report this.

734
00:30:53,067 --> 00:30:54,467
I really, really
have to report it.

735
