1455
01:01:06,867 --> 01:01:09,867
- [Mike] Oh, please, my
breasts are very sensitive.

1456
01:01:09,867 --> 01:01:10,700
- Oh yeah.

1457
01:01:12,067 --> 01:01:14,100
- Is the rest of the
equipment as good as that?

1458
01:01:15,767 --> 01:01:17,233
- [Guard] Let's have a look.

1459
01:01:17,233 --> 01:01:18,733
- What's he doing, Mike?
- Yeah.

1460
01:01:18,733 --> 01:01:21,033
- I don't think you guys--
- I'll make you a trade.

1461
01:01:21,033 --> 01:01:23,733
First your trousers.
- Just this part.

1462
01:01:23,733 --> 01:01:26,667
- And then you can
see everything.

1463
01:01:26,667 --> 01:01:28,967
- [Crow] This is supposed
to be an ipecac, right?

1464
01:01:30,000 --> 01:01:30,833
- Okay.

1465
01:01:32,433 --> 01:01:35,700
(suspenseful music)

1466
01:01:35,700 --> 01:01:37,500
- [Mike] That's the cast
of The Poseidon Adventure

1467
01:01:37,500 --> 01:01:38,533
coming the other way.

1468
01:01:40,567 --> 01:01:41,500
- [Tom] Oh jeez, the
guy's just coming down

1469
01:01:41,500 --> 01:01:43,033
to scoop out the cat box.

1470
01:01:44,833 --> 01:01:46,133
- [Mike] Look, I'm
sorry whoever you are,

1471
01:01:46,133 --> 01:01:48,167
I was just getting
really frustrated.

1472
01:01:48,167 --> 01:01:49,200
- No!
- No, no!

1473
01:01:50,133 --> 01:01:52,000
(stammering)
- I don't.

1474
01:01:52,000 --> 01:01:53,400
- Okay!
- It's all I got.

1475
01:01:55,900 --> 01:01:56,700
- My shoe.

1476
01:01:57,833 --> 01:01:58,867
- Shoe, shoe!

1477
01:01:59,733 --> 01:02:01,133
(all groaning)

1478
01:02:01,133 --> 01:02:02,100
- [Tom] Yuck.

1479
01:02:02,100 --> 01:02:03,600
(guard yelling)

1480
01:02:03,600 --> 01:02:05,933
- [Mike] Holy cow, that was
totally outta left field.

1481
01:02:07,967 --> 01:02:10,000
- Blast Thickneck.
- Crunch Buttsteak.

1482
01:02:10,000 --> 01:02:11,400
- [Mike] Slam Squattrust.

1483
01:02:13,100 --> 01:02:14,933
- [Tom] Oh, you lovable trollop.

1484
01:02:16,900 --> 01:02:18,500
- What took ya so long?

1485
01:02:18,500 --> 01:02:19,567
- I've been busy too.

1486
01:02:21,100 --> 01:02:22,400
Let's get his clothes.

1487
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:25,400
- [Crow] Oh, so it's
gonna be a three way.

1488
01:02:25,400 --> 01:02:27,233
Okay, that's fine, guys.

1489
01:02:27,233 --> 01:02:29,367
(door swishing)
- Rawhide.

1490
01:02:29,367 --> 01:02:30,967
(door swishing)
Rawhide.

1491
01:02:32,100 --> 01:02:33,300
(guard yelling)

1492
01:02:33,300 --> 01:02:34,833
- Let's go.

1493
01:02:34,833 --> 01:02:36,000
- [Tom] Come on,
I found this place

1494
01:02:36,000 --> 01:02:38,000
that makes these
really healthy shakes.

1495
01:02:40,400 --> 01:02:41,800
- Come on, move,
move, move, move!

1496
01:02:41,800 --> 01:02:43,900
Come on, move!
- I'm moving, bossy boots!

1497
01:02:46,233 --> 01:02:48,367
- [Mike] Come on, move, move,
move, you see how it feels?

1498
01:02:48,367 --> 01:02:49,200
Move!

1499
01:02:50,500 --> 01:02:51,667
- [Tom] Lump Beefbroth.

1500
01:02:54,733 --> 01:02:56,400
- [Crow] Move, move,
move, move, move!

1501
01:02:56,400 --> 01:02:58,000
- No, you move!
- No, you move, move!

1502
01:02:58,000 --> 01:02:59,700
- [Mike] No, you move!

1503
01:02:59,700 --> 01:03:01,667
- [Tom] Okay, now
move, move one leg

1504
01:03:01,667 --> 01:03:03,300
then move the other,
now breathe, breathe.

1505
01:03:03,300 --> 01:03:05,333
Now make your heart
beat, come on!

1506
01:03:05,333 --> 01:03:07,133
(suspenseful music)

1507
01:03:07,133 --> 01:03:09,433
- [Crow] You can see
right up their jumpsuits.

1508
01:03:12,433 --> 01:03:15,600
- [Mike] Did you sign Sherry's
belated birthday card?

1509
01:03:15,600 --> 01:03:17,100
- [Tom] Move, move, no, don't.

1510
01:03:22,833 --> 01:03:23,767
(man yelling)

1511
01:03:23,767 --> 01:03:25,000
- [Mike] How y'all doin'?

1512
01:03:26,433 --> 01:03:27,600
- [Crow] Ow, my mask!

1513
01:03:29,200 --> 01:03:30,967
- Here, put this on, okay?

1514
01:03:30,967 --> 01:03:32,667
- [Tom] But I just
loosed my hair.

1515
01:03:37,067 --> 01:03:40,533
- [Mike] These will make it
so we can't see anything.

1516
01:03:40,533 --> 01:03:44,567
- All right, let's move.

1517
01:03:44,567 --> 01:03:47,400
(muffled yelling)

1518
01:03:48,533 --> 01:03:50,433
- [Mike] The boiler
room has a receptionist?

1519
01:03:51,333 --> 01:03:52,767
- [Dave] All right, let's go.

1520
01:03:54,067 --> 01:03:55,500
- [Tom] And have
concluded that the boilers

1521
01:03:55,500 --> 01:03:57,000
have not moved for some time.

1522
01:03:57,000 --> 01:03:58,333
(computer beeping)

1523
01:03:58,333 --> 01:04:00,733
- [Guard] Hey, you
guys, let's see some ID.

1524
01:04:00,733 --> 01:04:02,800
- [Crow] Not technically a
railing but the same spirit.

1525
01:04:02,800 --> 01:04:03,967
- [Mike] Sure, sure.

1526
01:04:03,967 --> 01:04:05,400
(man groaning)

1527
01:04:05,400 --> 01:04:08,167
Ow, why do you hate
my groin so much?

1528
01:04:08,167 --> 01:04:09,300
- [Crow] I don't, Mike.

1529
01:04:09,300 --> 01:04:11,300
- Not you, Crow.
- All right, let's move.

1530
01:04:11,300 --> 01:04:12,933
- [Tom] I mean,
move, move, move!

1531
01:04:14,167 --> 01:04:15,567
- [Crow] Stupid freshmen!

1532
01:04:15,567 --> 01:04:17,367
- Have you located the girl?

1533
01:04:17,367 --> 01:04:18,500
- [Tom] I'll poke
my skull out at you!

1534
01:04:18,500 --> 01:04:19,333
- Answer me!

1535
01:04:21,300 --> 01:04:22,367
(growling)

1536
01:04:22,367 --> 01:04:24,833
I'm surrounded by incompetence!

1537
01:04:24,833 --> 01:04:27,367
I'm being undermined
by my own disciples!

1538
01:04:28,800 --> 01:04:30,933
You let that space bitch
slip through our fingers!

1539
01:04:30,933 --> 01:04:32,200
She was our--
- What do you call that?

1540
01:04:32,200 --> 01:04:34,400
- Where's that idiot
who let her escape?

1541
01:04:34,400 --> 01:04:35,733
- We've got him on ice, sir.

1542
01:04:35,733 --> 01:04:37,233
- Kill him at once!
- Yes sir.

1543
01:04:37,233 --> 01:04:39,667
- And then tell MacPhearson
our plan is operational.

1544
01:04:39,667 --> 01:04:41,567
Put the entire
squad on red alert!

1545
01:04:42,600 --> 01:04:43,833
(alarm blaring)

1546
01:04:43,833 --> 01:04:45,333
- [Crow] They woke up
the Oak Ridge Boys!

1547
01:04:45,333 --> 01:04:48,133
♪ Elvira ♪

1548
01:04:48,133 --> 01:04:50,800
(doors closing)

1549
01:04:59,933 --> 01:05:02,533
- Oh, say, that's a nice one.

1550
01:05:02,533 --> 01:05:03,600
Wrought iron.
- Hey Servo.

1551
01:05:03,600 --> 01:05:05,000
(yelling)

1552
01:05:05,000 --> 01:05:06,267
- Careful there, Mike.
- Another one of those things.

1553
01:05:06,267 --> 01:05:08,700
Servo, do you know
anything about this?

1554
01:05:08,700 --> 01:05:10,500
- Oh yeah, I just
installed a bunch

1555
01:05:10,500 --> 01:05:12,300
of new safety
railings on the ship.

1556
01:05:12,300 --> 01:05:13,933
- Oh really?
(laughing)

1557
01:05:13,933 --> 01:05:15,700
Why?
- Why?

1558
01:05:15,700 --> 01:05:17,367
What happens when OSHA stops by

1559
01:05:17,367 --> 01:05:19,600
and sees everything
completely unrailing, huh?

1560
01:05:19,600 --> 01:05:21,500
Big, fat fines, that's what!

1561
01:05:21,500 --> 01:05:22,767
But more importantly, Mike,

1562
01:05:22,767 --> 01:05:24,700
we've got to want to
do it for ourselves.

1563
01:05:24,700 --> 01:05:27,200
- But you can't just put
railings up randomly, I mean--

1564
01:05:27,200 --> 01:05:28,367
- You can't?
- There was a railing

1565
01:05:28,367 --> 01:05:30,067
in front of the door to my room.

1566
01:05:30,067 --> 01:05:32,567
There was an ankle-high
railing around the rugs.

1567
01:05:32,567 --> 01:05:35,333
And there was a railing around
the leftover hashbrowns.

1568
01:05:35,333 --> 01:05:36,833
I mean, ow!

1569
01:05:36,833 --> 01:05:38,500
- I better put a railing
around that railing there.

1570
01:05:38,500 --> 01:05:41,267
(Crow yelling)

1571
01:05:41,267 --> 01:05:43,933
Ah, Crow just found the
whisper-quiet high-speed

1572
01:05:43,933 --> 01:05:45,200
spinning spike railing.

1573
01:05:45,200 --> 01:05:47,233
- [Crow] Yeah, cool.

1574
01:05:47,233 --> 01:05:48,767
Ow.

1575
01:05:48,767 --> 01:05:50,600
- All right, Servo, you've
got one hour to get rid of

1576
01:05:50,600 --> 01:05:51,967
every railing on the ship, okay?

1577
01:05:51,967 --> 01:05:53,633
One hour, I mean it, all right?

1578
01:05:53,633 --> 01:05:55,100
- For crying out loud.

1579
01:05:55,100 --> 01:05:57,167
(Mike yelling)

1580
01:05:57,167 --> 01:05:58,833
Oh yeah, Mike, I
forgot to tell ya

1581
01:05:58,833 --> 01:06:00,833
that I had some moats put
in because it's pretty hard

1582
01:06:00,833 --> 01:06:02,900
to justify having
this many railings

1583
01:06:02,900 --> 01:06:05,800
without at least having some
big heights to have railings

1584
01:06:05,800 --> 01:06:08,133
in front of, know what I mean?

1585
01:06:08,133 --> 01:06:13,133
(water splashing)
- Servo!

1586
01:06:13,867 --> 01:06:15,633
- We'll be right back.

1587
01:06:15,633 --> 01:06:17,100
Hello!

1588
01:06:17,100 --> 01:06:19,667
(upbeat music)

1589
01:06:25,100 --> 01:06:27,100
- [Mike] Servo, there's
a railing around my seat.

1590
01:06:27,100 --> 01:06:27,933
- [Tom] You're welcome.

1591
01:06:27,933 --> 01:06:30,067
- Oh, thank God.

1592
01:06:30,067 --> 01:06:31,400
- [Mike] I'm okay too.

1593
01:06:33,500 --> 01:06:35,000
- [Crow] Hey, how 'bout
some sugar for Sting

1594
01:06:35,000 --> 01:06:36,900
and Dolph, here?

1595
01:06:36,900 --> 01:06:38,033
- Commander, we have a problem.

1596
01:06:38,033 --> 01:06:39,967
- I'm out of Mega Fuel.
- Yes, David?

1597
01:06:41,100 --> 01:06:42,733
- MacPhearson's a traitor.
- No.

1598
01:06:42,733 --> 01:06:45,300
- Yes, I saw him with Kalgan
at the Enforcer's headquarters.

1599
01:06:45,300 --> 01:06:48,000
- I can't believe it,
I mean it could be--

1600
01:06:48,000 --> 01:06:49,067
- Dad!

1601
01:06:49,067 --> 01:06:51,300
I saw him there today.
- Today?

1602
01:06:51,300 --> 01:06:53,100
- That being the
case, this is serious,

1603
01:06:53,100 --> 01:06:54,833
he knows our codes,
he has our weapons.

1604
01:06:54,833 --> 01:06:56,133
- Weapons?

1605
01:06:56,133 --> 01:06:58,400
- He knows all our
countermeasures.

1606
01:06:58,400 --> 01:06:59,900
- I find this unbelievable.

1607
01:06:59,900 --> 01:07:01,467
- [Tom] Wake up, Gramps.

1608
01:07:01,467 --> 01:07:03,700
- He's one of my best men,
he's my Chief Engineer.

1609
01:07:03,700 --> 01:07:05,033
- Commander, if I may say so--

1610
01:07:05,033 --> 01:07:06,267
- [Crow] You need
to cut some weight.

1611
01:07:06,267 --> 01:07:08,400
- Let me do my job.
- I'm coming with you.

1612
01:07:09,467 --> 01:07:11,333
- I'm coming too.
- I'm not.

1613
01:07:11,333 --> 01:07:13,600
- Captain, I'd
rather do it alone.

1614
01:07:13,600 --> 01:07:15,433
- As you please, Dave.
- But thank you.

1615
01:07:15,433 --> 01:07:16,933
- [Tom] You're welcome.

1616
01:07:16,933 --> 01:07:18,000
- Lea, you stay here.

1617
01:07:19,500 --> 01:07:21,167
Commander.

1618
01:07:21,167 --> 01:07:23,633
- [Mike] There goes a
big, brave brick of meat.

1619
01:07:25,000 --> 01:07:27,333
- [Crow] New, squid in a globe!

1620
01:07:27,333 --> 01:07:29,800
(mysterious music)

1621
01:07:29,800 --> 01:07:32,467
- [Tom] This is really hard
music to dance to, Cindy.

1622
01:07:33,733 --> 01:07:36,433
- [Mike] Laraine Newman
and the Newmanettes!

1623
01:07:36,433 --> 01:07:38,600
- [Jennera] One cannot
escape one's own destiny.

1624
01:07:38,600 --> 01:07:42,300
- [Crow] But one can delay it
indefinitely and have a beer.

1625
01:07:42,300 --> 01:07:43,900
(alarm blaring)

1626
01:07:43,900 --> 01:07:45,400
- We're going in!

1627
01:07:45,400 --> 01:07:47,200
- [Tom] I clogged up the
toilet but we're going in!

1628
01:07:48,400 --> 01:07:49,500
- [Mike] Aw, now they
stole the Enterprise's

1629
01:07:49,500 --> 01:07:50,967
red alert sound thingy.

1630
01:07:52,367 --> 01:07:54,000
- [Crow] Well, 86 the
pan-seared tuna, you guys,

1631
01:07:54,000 --> 01:07:55,233
chef says we're all out.

1632
01:07:56,733 --> 01:07:59,233
- [Tom] I'm gonna miss
this old wherever we are.

1633
01:08:02,300 --> 01:08:04,400
- [Mike] Don't get
smart with me, ceiling.

1634
01:08:07,667 --> 01:08:10,800
- Touch Rustrod.
- Reef Blastbody.

1635
01:08:10,800 --> 01:08:13,800
(suspenseful music)

1636
01:08:15,100 --> 01:08:17,100
- [Tom] Coach has us
doing wind sprints.

1637
01:08:20,433 --> 01:08:22,400
(vocalizing)

1638
01:08:22,400 --> 01:08:25,333
- [Tom] Sounds like Kitaro
fell asleep on his keyboard.

1639
01:08:25,333 --> 01:08:27,733
(vocalizing)

1640
01:08:31,667 --> 01:08:32,900
- [Mike] Big McLargeHuge.

1641
01:08:35,000 --> 01:08:36,200
- Damn you!

1642
01:08:36,200 --> 01:08:37,167
- [Crow] So where the
hell are these two

1643
01:08:37,167 --> 01:08:39,200
in relationship to each other?

1644
01:08:39,200 --> 01:08:40,333
- Sneaky little.

1645
01:08:43,033 --> 01:08:44,400
- Stop right there!

1646
01:08:44,400 --> 01:08:46,000
- [Tom] Would you like
to sample some Canoe?

1647
01:08:46,000 --> 01:08:47,467
- [Man] We're being
attacked from above,

1648
01:08:47,467 --> 01:08:49,067
Commander Ryder, we're
being attacked from above,

1649
01:08:49,067 --> 01:08:51,200
the Enforcers are--
(laser firing)

1650
01:08:51,200 --> 01:08:53,100
- [Crow] Hold on, let me
come down and tell you.

1651
01:08:53,100 --> 01:08:55,400
(man yelling)
Be right there.

1652
01:08:55,400 --> 01:08:58,167
(dramatic music)

1653
01:09:00,733 --> 01:09:03,033
- [Mike] Ow, jeez,
cut it out, you guys!

1654
01:09:03,033 --> 01:09:04,567
(lasers firing)

1655
01:09:04,567 --> 01:09:06,733
- [Crow] Here's little free
advice for the mutineers,

1656
01:09:06,733 --> 01:09:09,100
just stop and aim, you idiots!

1657
01:09:09,100 --> 01:09:10,800
- [Tom] Why is he so
impossible to hit?

1658
01:09:10,800 --> 01:09:13,600
Why do they keep on missing
the slow, giant white thing?

1659
01:09:15,300 --> 01:09:17,933
- He's going below!
- After him, move!

1660
01:09:17,933 --> 01:09:19,633
- Cut him off, hustle!

1661
01:09:22,233 --> 01:09:24,467
- [Mike] Loading up some
railing fodder here.

1662
01:09:26,800 --> 01:09:29,033
- [Crow] My flamethrower's
kinda weak here...

1663
01:09:30,967 --> 01:09:33,400
(vocalizing)

1664
01:09:35,300 --> 01:09:36,900
- Let's go, let's go!
- You know, in this movie

1665
01:09:36,900 --> 01:09:38,967
people don't seem to trust
other people's ability

1666
01:09:38,967 --> 01:09:43,867
to move forward.
- Yeah.

1667
01:09:43,867 --> 01:09:46,133
- [Crow] A horse, my
kingdom for a horse.

1668
01:09:46,133 --> 01:09:48,200
(lasers firing)

1669
01:09:48,200 --> 01:09:50,633
(vocalizing)

1670
01:09:52,933 --> 01:09:54,133
(man yelling)

1671
01:09:54,133 --> 01:09:56,267
- [Tom] Ooh, someone
get me a Zantac, quick!

1672
01:09:56,267 --> 01:09:59,233
- 300s.
(vocalizing)

1673
01:09:59,233 --> 01:10:01,033
- [Mike] Oh, send
my mask to Mother.

1674
01:10:03,067 --> 01:10:05,767
- [Crow] Stay together
cheeks, stay together cheeks.

1675
01:10:08,667 --> 01:10:10,200
- [Tom] Well, they rented
a pneumatic catapult

1676
01:10:10,200 --> 01:10:12,433
and damn it, they're
gonna use it.

1677
01:10:12,433 --> 01:10:15,500
- So many good lives wasted.
- Not these guy's lives.

1678
01:10:15,500 --> 01:10:20,133
- War always brings
out the worst in man.

1679
01:10:20,133 --> 01:10:21,200
I don't know.

1680
01:10:22,333 --> 01:10:24,600
I feel that I failed.
- You did, Daddy!

1681
01:10:24,600 --> 01:10:26,967
- Don't blame yourself,
it had to happen.

1682
01:10:26,967 --> 01:10:28,867
There was no compromise.

1683
01:10:28,867 --> 01:10:31,033
- [Tom] That scene really
makes me stop and think

1684
01:10:31,033 --> 01:10:34,033
about how much better a root
canal would be than this movie!

1685
01:10:37,500 --> 01:10:38,633
- [Mike] I think
they just borrowed

1686
01:10:38,633 --> 01:10:40,800
the South High
marching band uniforms.

1687
01:10:43,433 --> 01:10:45,900
- [Crow] So this takes place
at the Anheuser Busch brewery

1688
01:10:45,900 --> 01:10:47,500
or...

1689
01:10:47,500 --> 01:10:49,267
- [Mike] Oh, they're
having a craft fair.

1690
01:10:49,267 --> 01:10:52,233
(suspenseful music)

1691
01:10:53,733 --> 01:10:56,367
- [Tom] Giant toilet
seat hanging there.

1692
01:10:56,367 --> 01:10:59,133
- [Crow] Yeah, handicapped
accessible, I don't think so.

1693
01:11:00,433 --> 01:11:01,633
(laser firing)

1694
